 The infimum defining H^s_δ(E) is therefore finite. Discharge L5,L6 and quantify s,δ. Together with boundedness in S001 and F003 this is the asserted conclusion.", "uses": ["H002"], "uses_local": ["F003"], "objects": ["E", "n", "s", "δ", "H", "diam", "D"], "produces": [], "introduces": ["L5", "L6"], "discharges": ["L5", "L6"]}], "applications": []}, "has_more": false, "next_offset": null}, {"id": "nl0.json", "pointer": "/inferences/2", "view": "value", "value": {"id": "R003", "inputs": ["N001"], "output": "N003", "definitions": ["D001", "D002", "D004", "D005", "D008"], "rules": ["direct", "forall_introduction", "implication_introduction"], "locals": [{"symbol": "a", "type": "real number", "scope": "R003/argument", "start": "S001", "end": "S001", "kind": "arbitrary", "declaration": "Fix a real exponent a.", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": []}, {"symbol": "N", "type": "positive integer", "scope": "R003/argument", "start": "S001", "end": "S001", "kind": "arbitrary", "declaration": "Let N range over positive integers.", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": []}, {"symbol": "s", "type": "real number", "scope": "R003/argument", "start": "S002", "end": "S004", "kind": "arbitrary", "declaration": "Fix a real exponent s.", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": []}, {"symbol": "δ", "type": "real number", "scope": "R003/argument", "start": "S002", "end": "S004", "kind": "arbitrary", "declaration": "Fix a real scale δ.", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": []}, {"symbol": "K", "type": "subset of ℕ", "scope": "R003/argument", "start": "S002", "end": "S003", "kind": "arbitrary", "declaration": "Use K⊆ℕ to index the nonempty members of an arbitrary countable cover.", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": []}, {"symbol": "V", "type": "family of nonempty subsets of ℝ indexed by K", "scope": "R003/argument", "start": "S002", "end": "S003", "kind": "arbitrary", "declaration": "Fix an arbitrary covering family V indexed by K.", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": ["K"]}, {"symbol": "ρ", "type": "nonnegative real family indexed by K", "scope": "R003/argument", "start": "S002", "end": "S003", "kind": "definition", "declaration": "Put ρ_i=diam(V_i) for i∈K.", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": ["K", "V", "diam"]}, {"symbol": "ε", "type": "real number", "scope": "R003/argument", "start": "S002", "end": "S002", "kind": "arbitrary", "declaration": "Fix a real error ε.", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": []}, {"symbol": "J", "type": "family of open intervals indexed by K", "scope": "R003/argument", "start": "S002", "end": "S002", "kind": "definition", "declaration": "For each i∈K put J_i=(inf V_i-ε2^(-i-2), sup V_i+ε2^(-i-2)). This is used under the bounded nonempty-cover and ε>0 conditions.", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": ["K", "V", "ε"]}], "argument": [{"id": "S001", "text": "Fix a>1 (temporary assumption L1). Partition I into N equal closed intervals, N a positive integer. Their diameters are 1/N and their total a-cost is N(1/N)^a=N^(1-a)→0 as N→∞. For every positive target scale these covers are eventually admissible and have costs tending to zero. Thus H^a(I)=0; N001 gives dim_H(I)≤a for every a>1, and hence dim_H(I)≤1. Discharge L1. Record F001: H^a(I)=0 for every a>1 and dim_H(I)≤1.", "uses": ["N001"], "uses_local": [], "objects": ["I", "a", "N", "H", "dim_H", "diam"], "produces": [{"id": "F001", "statement": "For every a_b>1, H^a_b(I)=0, and dim_H(I)≤1.", "objects": ["I", "H", "dim_H", "a_b"], "binders": [{"symbol": "a_b", "type": "real number"}], "assumptions": []}], "introduces": ["L1"], "discharges": ["L1"]}, {"id": "S002", "text": "Fix s,δ, and assume L2: 0<s<1 and L3: δ>0. Consider any countable δ-cover V of I, with nonempty members indexed by K⊆ℕ after discarding empty members; assume this cover condition as L4. Put ρ_i=diam(V_i)≤δ. Fix ε>0 (L5). Each V_i is bounded and nonempty, so inf V_i and sup V_i exist and sup V_i-inf V_i=ρ_i. Define J_i=(inf V_i-ε2^(-i-2),sup V_i+ε2^(-i-2)). Then V_i⊆J_i and |J_i|=ρ_i+ε2^(-i-1). Countable subadditivity of Lebesgue measure, applied to the open intervals covering I, gives 1=|I|≤sum_{i∈K}|J_i|≤sum_{i∈K}ρ_i+ε because sum_{i≥0}2^(-i-1)=1. If sum ρ_i=∞ the required inequality is automatic; otherwise let ε↓0 to obtain sum ρ_i≥1. Discharge L5. Record F002: sum_{i∈K}ρ_i≥1.", "uses": [], "uses_local": [], "objects": ["s", "δ", "I", "K", "V", "ρ", "ε", "J", "λ", "diam"], "produces": [{"id": "F002", "statement": "sum_{i∈K}ρ_i≥1.", "objects": ["K", "ρ"], "binders": [], "assumptions": ["L2", "L3", "L4"]}], "introduces": ["L2", "L3", "L4", "L5"], "discharges": ["L5"]}, {"id": "S003", "text": "For each i∈K with ρ_i>0, ρ_i≤δ and s-1<0 imply ρ_i^s=ρ_i·ρ_i^(s-1)≥δ^(s-1)ρ_i. For ρ_i=0 both sides are zero since s>0. Summing nonnegative terms and using F002 gives sum_{i∈K}ρ_i^s≥δ^(s-1)sum_{i∈K}ρ_i≥δ^(s-1). This is true of every δ-cover. Discharge the arbitrary-cover assumption L4 and take the infimum to get F003: H^s_δ(I)≥δ^(s-1).", "uses": [], "uses_local": ["F002"], "objects": ["K", "ρ", "s", "δ", "H", "I"], "produces": [{"id": "F003", "statement": "H^s_δ(I)≥δ^(s-1).", "objects": ["H", "I", "s", "δ"], "binders": [], "assumptions": ["L2", "L3"]}], "introduces": [], "discharges": ["L4"]}, {"id": "S004", "text": "The bound F003 holds at every δ>0. Since s-1<0, δ^(s-1)→∞ as δ↓0. Thus H^s(I)=∞, and N001 implies dim_H(I)≥s for every 0<s<1. Taking s↑1 gives dim_H(I)≥1; together with F001 this gives dim_H(I)=1 and all the explicit measure clauses of the asserted conclusion. Discharge L2,L3 and universally quantify the indicated exponents and scales.", "uses": ["N001"], "uses_local": ["F001", "F003"], "objects": ["s", "δ", "I", "H", "dim_H"], "produces": [], "introduces": [], "discharges": ["L2", "L3"]}], "applications": []}, "has_more": false, "next_offset": null}], "has_more": false, "next_request": null, "total_requests": 3}
